It's for the #version command in the tty NetHack.exe. Not having
it means that you get an error message and some screen munge
in the tty version, but nothing worse. The ttyoptions and
guioptions files tell you what options you have compiled into
your executable--or, in this case, *my* executable. Since I only
built NetHackW.exe (which is effortless with MSVC++), only
guioptions made it into my nhdat.

Thanks for noticing this. I guess this means that I can't get
a fully correct nhdat file unless I build both, or cheat
by putting the vanilla ttyoptions file in my dat/ directory
and letting it get swept up into the build. Which I just did.

